{
  "dom_id": "step-36411",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Computing the Linear Correlation Coefficient Using the Expanded Formula",
  "problem": "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx = \\big\\{ 13, \\: 10, \\: 9, \\: 12 \\big\\},\\qquad\ny = \\big\\{ -1, \\: 3, \\: 2, \\: 4 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nYou are given that $\\overline{x}=11$ and $\\overline{y}=2.$ Calculate the corresponding linear correlation coefficient. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "The linear correlation coefficient $\\rho$ of the data sets $x=\\big\\{ x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}$ and $y=\\big\\{ y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\rho(x,y) =  \\dfrac{\\textrm{Cov}(x,y)}{\\sigma_x \\cdot \\sigma_y} = \\dfrac{S_{xy}}{\\sqrt{S_{xx} \\cdot S_{yy}}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(13-11)(-1-2)+(10-11)(3-2) \\\\  & +(9-11)(2-2)+(12-11)(4-2) \\\\  & =(2)(-3)+(-1)(1)+(-2)(0)+(1)(2) \\\\  & =-6-1+0+2 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we compute the sums in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(13-11)^{2}+(10-11)^{2}+(9-11)^{2}+(12-11)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+4+1 \\\\  & =10 \\\\ {S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & =(-1-2)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =9+1+0+4 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho (x,y) & =\\frac{(-5)}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & ≈-\\frac{5}{3.162\\,278\\cdot 3.741\\,657} \\\\  & ≈-0.42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
